---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConversionActions from '../components/ConversionActions.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="PostgreSQL Consulting Pricing: Fixed-Price Reviews | WalStack" description="Start with a free snapshot. A slowdown investigation costs $450 for my first 3 clients, then $750. See upgrade pricing and exactly what each review includes.">
  <header class="container hero"><h1>PostgreSQL review pricing</h1><p class="lede">Start with three written findings for free. If you need a deeper answer, here’s what it costs in USD.</p></header>
  <section><div class="container">
    <div class="table-wrap pricing-table"><table><caption class="visually-hidden">PostgreSQL review prices in USD</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Review</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">What you get</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/snapshot">Free snapshot review</a></th><td>$0</td><td>3 written findings within 2 business days of acceptance, from one read-only script. Up to {site.snapshotMonthlyCap} a month, for companies running PostgreSQL in production.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">Postgres Slowdown Investigation</a></th><td>{site.investigationOffer.display}</td><td>The cause, a safe fix, a review call and a 14-day check. Full refund if the report has no recommendation backed by evidence from your system.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">PostgreSQL Upgrade Readiness</a></th><td>{site.upgradeOffer.display}</td><td>Pre-upgrade checks, current query timings, a comparison plan and a rollback plan.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>After an investigation, you can ask me about a monthly check-in.</p>
    <div class="prose"><h2>Which one to start with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Production is slow now and you don't know why:</strong> send the free snapshot. If the findings point to a deeper cause, the <a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">slowdown audit</a> follows the same evidence.</li>
      <li><strong>You already know the problem is worth a paid answer:</strong> book the audit directly. It covers one production database.</li>
      <li><strong>You are planning a major-version upgrade:</strong> the <a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">upgrade readiness assessment</a> covers compatibility and regression risk. The snapshot looks only at today's workload.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Payment and timing</h2>
    <p>I invoice upfront in USD and confirm payment details before you commit. The audit report arrives 3 business days after I get read-only access or your script output. Founding prices apply to the first clients only, and the standard price is shown next to each one.</p><ConversionActions /></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
